# ripgrep/fd search-exclusions (does NOT affect git tracking).
# The archive holds frozen historical source provenance; excluding it keeps
# `rg` focused on active source and avoids matching superseded/duplicate copies.
# To search archive explicitly: `rg --no-ignore <pattern> workspace/public/archive`
workspace/public/archive/

# Superseded docs and reports. Location is the authority signal: a file under
# docs/archive/ is historical and must not be read as current state. Excluding
# it here stops a search from returning a stale frontier next to the live one.
docs/archive/
